1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,730
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:10,650
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,470
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:17,350
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:21,520
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:32,090
Go back to the sheath that protects you.

7
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,770
Go back to Griffith!

8
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:50,550
Don't glower at me like that.

9
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:56,240
I'm offering you all the fun you want
right before setting out for the afterlife.

10
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:08,500
What's wrong?
Are you embarrassed?

11
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:18,410
I'm unable to push this bastard aside...

12
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:20,050
Why...

13
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,380
Why is my arm so powerless...

14
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:53,550
Feel no shame about shape

15
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:55,460
Weather changes their phrase

16
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:59,220
Even mother will show you another way

17
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,600
So put your glasses on

18
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,680
Nothing will be wrong

19
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,890
There's no blame. There's no fame

20
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:07,730
It's up to you

21
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:11,360
The first words should be found

22
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,980
Whatever holds you back

23
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:16,360
I...

24
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:17,490
...can...

25
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:19,660
I can get it off

26
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:20,660
Tell me what...

27
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:21,660
Tell me what...

28
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,490
Tell me what you want

29
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:24,580
I don't know why...

30
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:25,580
Don't know why...

31
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,580
Don't know why you're afraid

32
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:28,750
Tell me what...

33
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:29,710
Tell me what...

34
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,380
Tell me what you'd say

35
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,710
I don't know why...

36
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:33,790
Don't know why...

37
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:34,590
Too late...

38
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:36,210
It's too late

39
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:45,140
Bonfire of Dreams

40
00:02:56,780 --> 00:03:00,990
Don't even think about
biting your tongue off.

41
00:03:00,990 --> 00:03:04,200
It'd be a shame if you died
before we finished our fun.

42
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:11,420
Do you want to die in a place like this?

43
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:16,380
Go back to the sheath that protects you.

44
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,800
I won't bite my tongue off.

45
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:23,260
Oh no, she's been driven to despair.

46
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:26,890
Can't you resist a little
so we can get turned on?

47
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:28,930
But...

48
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:31,190
I won't let you rape me either!

49
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:32,190
What?

50
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:36,110
Bitch!

51
00:03:36,110 --> 00:03:37,610
You'll pay for that!

52
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,080
I'll kill you!

53
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,130
You better lay off now.

54
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:02,090
Judeau!

55
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:04,890
She's the only woman in our troop.

56
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,970
It'll cost you.

57
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,860
Unbelievable!

58
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:22,070
He's beaten almost half my hundred
men in spite of his wounds...

59
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:24,990
I admit this is no fluke.

60
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:27,070
What was that?

61
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,200
There are fifty of you still alive?

62
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:35,620
It'll be dawn by the time I get
around to cracking all your heads.

63
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:39,960
Don't let up!

64
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,880
He barely has the strength to stand!

65
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,130
Defeat him now!

66
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:58,980
What am I doing here?

67
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,230
In a miserable place like this...

68
00:05:06,030 --> 00:05:08,240
It's not worth risking my life for this...

69
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:10,910
Am I fighting for Casca?

70
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,370
No, that can't be it...

71
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:21,250
I don't have time to think now.

72
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:23,670
I should concentrate on wielding my sword...

73
00:05:24,510 --> 00:05:25,550
...and killing...

74
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:26,630
Nothing more...

75
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:39,440
Sorry I was late.

76
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:43,280
It took quite a while to persuade those
big shots we needed to rescue you.

77
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,200
H-Hey...

78
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:48,360
You must run...

79
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:50,780
He...

80
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:51,950
Guts...

81
00:05:52,450 --> 00:05:53,290
Hurry!

82
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:55,080
What happened to Guts?

83
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:57,410
This way, quickly!

84
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:00,250
Someone, give her your shoulder!

85
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,210
I don't need it!

86
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,250
He...

87
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:07,720
He stayed to fight the enemy
alone so that I could get away...

88
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:10,090
We've got to hurry, or...

89
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:15,970
Let's move!

90
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,560
Let us get there in time...

91
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,770
Please let us get there in time!

92
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:36,450
Here it is!

93
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,800
Oh, my God...

94
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:57,100
Is this for real?

95
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:59,060
I see almost a hundred men lying here.

96
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,190
Did he really do all this by himself?

97
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:17,540
Guts...

98
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:21,330
Guts!

99
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,020
Guts!

100
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:42,850
Guts!

101
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:43,400
Guts!
Those look like fatal wounds...

102
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,190
Those look like fatal wounds...

103
00:07:44,190 --> 00:07:45,230
Guts!

104
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:47,230
Come on, you're only joking, right?

105
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:48,530
Hey, Guts!

106
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,030
Guts!

107
00:07:50,650 --> 00:07:51,700
Guts!

108
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,000
Stop shaking me...

109
00:08:00,910 --> 00:08:03,170
It'll aggravate my wounds.

110
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,580
Guts...

111
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:08,250
Out of the way now!

112
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:09,340
Move it!

113
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,010
It's an emergency!

114
00:08:11,010 --> 00:08:12,010
Make way for us!

115
00:08:12,010 --> 00:08:13,880
It's no big deal!

116
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,220
I can walk on my own!

117
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:17,180
Don't move. Your injuries will worsen!

118
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:19,220
Hey, they're back!

119
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,310
Damn it, he is alive after all.

120
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:23,440
Guts!

121
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:26,770
Hey, ouch!

122
00:08:26,770 --> 00:08:28,320
That hurts!

123
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:32,320
You'll heal faster without
anesthetic, so just bear it.

124
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,740
Shit!

125
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:35,570
I'm not a torn shirt you're sewing up!

126
00:08:35,910 --> 00:08:38,030
Okay, I'm done now.

127
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:42,200
What a guy!

128
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:47,630
With wounds like yours, most men
wouldn't be able to stay conscious.

129
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,380
How's his condition?

130
00:08:49,710 --> 00:08:54,760
Well, he's no longer in danger,
but I prescribe total bed rest for him!

131
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:56,640
Total bed rest?

132
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:59,600
Then what you're saying is...

133
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:03,680
In other words, he should not
continue on this expedition.

134
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:04,690
No way!

135
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:06,020
Bullshit!

136
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,610
I'll stick with you all until the end,
even if I have to crawl after you!

137
00:09:08,610 --> 00:09:09,900
Ridiculous!

138
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:12,820
If you go back into battle,
I can't guarantee your survival.

139
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:15,450
Guarantee my survival?

140
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:17,990
Whoever heard of a thing like that in battle?

141
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:19,780
It's out of the question!

142
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,780
Oh, suit yourself!

143
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,790
Oh, well... We should be
happy things ended up this way!

144
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:33,300
The two of you are back safe and sound.

145
00:09:37,470 --> 00:09:39,050
Where is Griffith, anyway?

146
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:42,140
Griffith is at headquarters for the war council.

147
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,810
He set out this morning.

148
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:44,810
Oh no.

149
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:47,100
He won't come back until tomorrow.

150
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:51,570
And they finally came back too.

151
00:09:51,570 --> 00:09:53,190
What bad timing!

152
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,650
Casca, aren't you going to get looked at?

153
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:00,160
I'm fine.

154
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,370
After all... it's not as though I got wounded.

155
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,790
But you had a fever, didn't you?

156
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:08,620
Oh!

157
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:10,080
What's going on?

158
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:26,020
Seriously, we were worried that
the worst might have happened.

159
00:10:26,310 --> 00:10:30,350
For once, we need
to thank Commander Guts.

160
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:32,900
Sorry for having worried you all.

161
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:34,690
I'm glad you're safe, big sister.

162
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,400
But Captain Griffith is cold at heart.

163
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,490
Even if he did have to attend
a war council or whatever...

164
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:42,740
Watch your mouth.

165
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,660
Oh, I am sorry, big sister...

166
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:47,830
Casca.

167
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:50,580
Can I have your ear for a moment?

168
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:56,760
What's the matter?

169
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:59,720
Well, I want to tell you this.

170
00:11:01,890 --> 00:11:06,680
When I asked Griffith to send
a search party to rescue you two...

171
00:11:07,430 --> 00:11:11,230
...those nobles spoke against us,
making objections of all kinds.

172
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:13,440
But...

173
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,190
Griffith really put his foot down.

174
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:19,280
Those two are key to us.

175
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,280
I cannot afford to lose them.

176
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,990
Griffith said that...

177
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,080
That's right. My hat's off to you two.

178
00:11:26,410 --> 00:11:28,750
To think that he values you so much
he'd say something like that!

179
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:32,960
Honestly, I felt a little jealous.

180
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,470
Oh, hey, I almost forgot about this.

181
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:50,140
Give this to the big guy
who killed a hundred men.

182
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:51,940
It's medicine?

183
00:11:53,310 --> 00:11:56,570
I got this from a company of
traveling players I used to work for.

184
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:58,900
You may not believe it...

185
00:11:59,230 --> 00:12:01,650
...but it is made from fairy dust.

186
00:12:01,650 --> 00:12:02,820
Fairy dust?

187
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,360
That's impossible!

188
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,910
I know you doubt it.

189
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:09,290
But it works wonders,
and the effect is guaranteed.

190
00:12:09,290 --> 00:12:12,750
It saved my life
a couple of times. Trust me.

191
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:15,040
Such a precious thing of yours...

192
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:16,670
Don't worry.

193
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:21,130
I think it's a fairly good deal, a hundred
men for one pack of medicine.

194
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,100
Thank you, Judeau.

195
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:39,020
She's acting so girlish all of a sudden...

196
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,070
Guts...

197
00:13:08,470 --> 00:13:09,510
Guts...

198
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,210
What's going on?

199
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:42,340
Wouldn't it be better if you slept?

200
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,510
I can't sleep because my body is burning.

201
00:13:50,050 --> 00:13:53,310
Up here I feel at ease, and it's much cooler.

202
00:13:59,190 --> 00:14:00,110
Hey...

203
00:14:00,110 --> 00:14:01,060
Don't move.

204
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,630
The pain...

205
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:22,790
...is subsiding.

206
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:26,920
What is this?

207
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:28,880
Judeau gave it to me.

208
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,140
It's some kind of secret medicine.

209
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,310
Now turn your back.

210
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:43,570
You know...

211
00:14:43,570 --> 00:14:45,400
...there's nothing for you
to worry yourself over.

212
00:14:46,530 --> 00:14:48,900
I only did that for my own sake.

213
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,820
It wasn't for you in particular.

214
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:59,580
I'd rather fight with my sword
than run away. It's my nature.

215
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,460
That was the only reason...

216
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:07,170
You fought a hundred men with
your sword because it's your nature?

217
00:15:13,350 --> 00:15:15,390
Yeah, that's it.

218
00:15:16,890 --> 00:15:19,730
Besides, I had to give that bastard some payback.

219
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:24,560
I don't recall anything clearly since
I was caught up in swinging my sword.

220
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:32,110
But to tell you the truth, I couldn't
get something out of my head...

221
00:15:32,610 --> 00:15:34,870
Fighting against a hundred men...

222
00:15:35,330 --> 00:15:37,660
...means nothing...

223
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:39,160
...compared to what you are doing.

224
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:51,930
Not only you, but Griffith too...

225
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:56,350
You two have something important
enough to stake your lives on.

226
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:59,390
I think it's great. I mean it.

227
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:03,980
Compared to your purpose...

228
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:08,530
...my random battles against
a hundred men or even a thousand...

229
00:16:08,530 --> 00:16:09,690
...seem insignificant.

230
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:11,900
Guts...

231
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,780
Some view, huh?

232
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,790
Gaston doesn't think
he's very suited to army life.

233
00:16:23,210 --> 00:16:24,870
After the war...

234
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:28,090
...he wants to start a tailoring
business with the money he's earned.

235
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:31,130
He's good with his hands,
though he may not look like it.

236
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:34,590
Nichol proposed to a woman, but she refused.

237
00:16:34,590 --> 00:16:37,430
She didn't want to marry a common soldier.

238
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:40,350
He wants to get promoted as soon
as possible so he can ask her again.

239
00:16:41,350 --> 00:16:44,270
That's why he is reckless and
tends to overextend himself in battle.

240
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:49,110
It seems that everyone is still
betting on their unrequited hopes.

241
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:59,530
Looking over all of them from here,
it makes me think that I can see...

242
00:16:59,990 --> 00:17:03,460
...their little dreams and hopes...

243
00:17:03,790 --> 00:17:05,540
...flickering in each light.

244
00:17:10,550 --> 00:17:13,840
Like a bonfire of dreams...

245
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:16,590
That was beautiful...

246
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:18,600
I thought it was the princess talking.

247
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,350
Don't say that!

248
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:23,060
But you're right.

249
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,390
I think that each one of them...

250
00:17:25,390 --> 00:17:29,900
...shine their own wisps of light
when they gather together.

251
00:17:30,270 --> 00:17:36,150
Yeah, and to keep those
faint lights from withering out...

252
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:39,870
...they join their light with
the strongest flame of all...

253
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:46,370
A powerful fire called Griffith...

254
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:50,920
But...

255
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:53,090
...you won't find my light among them.

256
00:17:56,470 --> 00:18:03,100
I guess I'm just someone who
stopped to warm up by the bonfire.

257
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:04,640
Guts...

258
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:14,320
As long as I have my sword to fight
with, I know I can survive any battle.

259
00:18:15,190 --> 00:18:17,610
That's how it's always
turned out for me till now.

260
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:23,120
Before joining the Band of
the Hawk, I alone always survived...

261
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:25,290
...even in hopeless, losing battles.

262
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:27,290
It happened again this time...

263
00:18:28,410 --> 00:18:32,630
But you know, surviving these
battles really doesn't mean anything.

264
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,670
I've been fighting for as long as I can remember.

265
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:40,010
The mercenary leader who raised me...

266
00:18:40,010 --> 00:18:43,100
...taught me nothing except
how to wield a sword.

267
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:46,600
I've never had anything except my sword.

268
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:48,940
I don't want to die.

269
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,150
But even still, throughout all this time...

270
00:18:52,690 --> 00:18:55,530
I continue to fight...

271
00:18:56,230 --> 00:18:58,280
...because wielding a sword is all I know.

272
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:05,160
Back there, I was ready
to commit myself solely to fighting...

273
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:09,000
...and leave it to others
to find a real reason to fight for.

274
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:10,870
Guts...

275
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:16,420
Anyway, I guess all that
sounds kind of dumb.

276
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:18,550
I'm wondering why I told you all that...

277
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,470
Pretty pathetic.

278
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,180
I'm wondering the same thing.

279
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,220
Guts...

280
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,730
...are you thinking of...

281
00:19:36,730 --> 00:19:40,490
Are you going to leave
the Band of the Hawk?

282
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:51,870
Guts...

283
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:56,540
I said that I was going to fight in
this war until the end, no matter what.

284
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:59,260
What will you do afterwards?

285
00:19:59,710 --> 00:20:01,170
Guts!

286
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:02,090
Casca!

287
00:20:04,510 --> 00:20:05,970
Griffith is back!

288
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,470
He heard that you were safe...

289
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:11,060
...so he changed his schedule
to come back here a day early!

290
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,690
Welcome back!

291
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,070
Captain!

292
00:20:19,070 --> 00:20:19,940
Glad you're safe!

293
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,440
Oh, Commander Guts!

294
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:28,530
Hey.

295
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,460
Griffith, I apologize.

296
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:40,340
I held everyone back. It's my fault...

297
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:43,170
Despite my physical condition...

298
00:20:43,170 --> 00:20:45,930
...I went into battle and
made a mess of things.

299
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:48,680
I even put my entire company in danger.

300
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:52,310
Not only that, I put Guts
and his Raiders at risk as well.

301
00:20:52,770 --> 00:20:54,810
I'm not qualified to be a commander!

302
00:20:54,810 --> 00:20:55,980
I will accept any punishment...

303
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:59,230
W-What are you doing, you idiot!

304
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,530
Welcome back.

305
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,910
Go for it, Commander!

306
00:21:15,830 --> 00:21:17,540
Jump on me too!

307
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:19,960
All right, let's all go and get a drink!

308
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,300
Are you sure, Commander?

309
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,760
In your condition?

310
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:26,550
Shut up, the alcohol will
disinfect my body from the inside!

311
00:21:26,550 --> 00:21:28,260
I'm not responsible for this.

312
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,970
Let's celebrate the hundred-man fight!

313
00:21:30,810 --> 00:21:31,720
What's the matter?

314
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:33,890
Nothing...

315
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:35,980
Is he...

316
00:21:36,770 --> 00:21:38,310
...serious about leaving?

317
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

318
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

319
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

320
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

321
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

322
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

323
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

324
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

325
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

326
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

327
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

